<title>SOUTH AFRICA: T&amp;N year earnings slide, dividend cut.</title>
<headline>T&amp;N year earnings slide, dividend cut.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Dec 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     90.7	  vs 173.5</p>
<p>    Final div (cts)	 13.0	  vs 33.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   22.1	  vs 40.8</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   25.9	  vs 56.1</p>
<p>    Tax			 3.8	   vs 15.3</p>
<p>    Turnover		  823.1	 vs 727.5</p>
<p>Full name: T&amp;N Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The engineering firm said that it resolved to issue new ordinary shares as a capitalisation share award to ordinary shareholders registered on March 20. Shareholders can select a cash alternative.</p>
<p>The firm said the profit slump in the period was due to higher interest rates and increased borrowing and the acquisition of its Connoisseur unit.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
